        "8460": {"synopsis":"$FDAE = the next place; bank 7.","comment":"DE = the next place"},
        "8461": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack ($05D1)"},
        "8464": {"comment":"$FDAE = it"},
        "8468": {"comment":"Done"},
        "8469": {"synopsis":"Whether BC bytes fit between STKEND and the stack, with $82 bytes to spare; returns with\ncarry when they do. Otherwise ERR_NR = 3 and REPORT_4_ROOM (report 4, \"MEMORIA AGOTADA\" in\nthis set's ROM 3).","comment":"HL = STKEND + BC"},
        "8473": {"comment":"Past $FFFF?"},
        "8475": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "8476": {"comment":"Plus $82 to spare"},
        "8480": {"comment":"Past $FFFF?"},
        "8482": {"comment":"Below SP?"},
        "8484": {"comment":"Yes: carry, they fit"},
        "8485": {"synopsis":"No room: ERR_NR = 3 (report 4), then ROM 1's $2747 through $3E80, which calls the ROM 1\nroutine whose address is the word after the CALL.","comment":"ERR_NR = 3: report 4"},
        "8490": {"comment":"To ROM 1's $2747 (the word after the CALL)"},
        "8495": {"synopsis":"Looks the word in the buffer at $FDA0 up as a keyword, letters in either case:\n1. $1449 copies the RAM routines to $FCAE again ($E8 bytes from $145E), clearing $FC9F and\n$FCA1.\n2. ROM 3's keywords: the RAM routine at $FD43 (the copy of $14DC) pages ROM 3 in and looks\nthrough its list at $0096, codes from $A5.\n3. Then this ROM's list at $16AA (the RAM routine at $FD5C, the copy of $150C, B = $F9):\nSPECTRUM, PLAY, GOTO, GOSUB, DEFFN, OPEN#, CLOSE# (the spellings as stored there), which\ngive $A3, $A4, $EC (GO TO), $ED (GO SUB), $CE (DEF FN), $D3 (OPEN #), $D4 (CLOSE #).\nExit: carry and A = the token when found; no carry otherwise.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The RAM routines copied to $FCAE again ($1449)"},
        "8498": {"comment":"ROM 3's keywords (the RAM routine at $FD43)"},
        "8501": {"comment":"Found: carry, A = the token"},
        "8502": {"comment":"The 128K's own list, codes from $F9"},
        "8504": {"comment":"DE = the word"},
        "8507": {"comment":"HL = the 128K's list"},
        "8510": {"comment":"Looked up (the RAM routine at $FD5C)"},
        "8513": {"comment":"Not found: no carry"},
        "8514": {"comment":"$FF: CLOSE # ($D4)?"},
        "8516": {"comment":"No: KW_NOT_FF"},
        "8518": {"comment":"The CLOSE # token"},
        "8520": {"comment":"Found"},
        "8522": {"synopsis":"$FE: OPEN # ($D3)?"},
        "8524": {"comment":"No: KW_NOT_FE"},
        "8526": {"comment":"The OPEN # token"},
        "8528": {"comment":"Found"},
        "8530": {"synopsis":"$FD: DEF FN ($CE)?"},
        "8532": {"comment":"No: KW_NOT_FD"},
        "8534": {"comment":"The DEF FN token"},
        "8536": {"comment":"Found"},
        "8538": {"synopsis":"$FC: GO SUB ($ED)?"},
        "8540": {"comment":"No: KW_NOT_FC"},
        "8542": {"comment":"The GO SUB token"},
        "8544": {"comment":"Found"},
        "8546": {"synopsis":"$FB: GO TO ($EC)?"},
        "8548": {"comment":"No: KW_NOT_FB"},
        "8550": {"comment":"The GO TO token"},
        "8552": {"comment":"Found"},
        "8554": {"synopsis":"$F9 or $FA: less $56 (SPECTRUM $A3, PLAY $A4).","comment":"$A3 SPECTRUM or $A4 PLAY"},
        "8556": {"synopsis":"Carry: found."},
        "8557": {"comment":"Back with the token"},
        "8558": {"synopsis":"Copies the bytes at HL, a count first, to DE.\nExit: HL and DE past them; B = 0.","comment":"B = the count"},
        "8560": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"Copied"},
        "8562": {"comment":"Both on"},
        "8564": {"comment":"All?"},
        "8566": {"comment":"Done"},
        "8567": {"synopsis":"Carry and A = its value when A is a digit '0'-'9'; no carry otherwise. Nothing in this ROM\ncalls it.","comment":"Below '0'?"},
        "8570": {"comment":"Yes: no carry"},
        "8571": {"comment":"Past '9'?"},
        "8573": {"comment":"Yes: no carry"},
        "8574": {"comment":"A = its value"},
        "8576": {"comment":"Carry: a digit"},
        "8578": {"synopsis":"Looks key A up in the table at HL (a count, then code and address per key) and runs the\nroutine found.\nExit: no carry and NZ when not found; Z when found, carry as the routine\nreturned it.","comment":"BC and DE kept"},
        "8580": {"comment":"B = the count"},
        "8582": {"synopsis":"The next entry: its code compared with A.","comment":"This key?"},
        "8583": {"comment":"DE = the entry's address"},
        "8587": {"comment":"Yes: TABLE_FOUND"},
        "8589": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8590": {"comment":"The next"},
        "8592": {"comment":"Not found: no carry"},
        "8594": {"comment":"DE and BC back"},
        "8597": {"synopsis":"Found: the routine run (TABLE_CALL), Z, its carry kept.","comment":"HL = the routine"},
        "8598": {"comment":"DE and BC back"},
        "8600": {"comment":"Run (TABLE_CALL)"},
        "8603": {"comment":"It returned carry?"},
        "8605": {"comment":"Z and no carry"},
        "8607": {"synopsis":"The routine returned carry: Z and carry.","comment":"Z"},
        "8608": {"comment":"And carry"},
        "8610": {"synopsis":"Jumps to HL."},
        "8611": {"synopsis":"The routine ROM 2 reaches through this ROM's $3FF0 (ROM2_HOOK) when it asks about a disk.\nUnlike the English ROM it is given no text: it prints its own Spanish ones, in the lower\nscreen:\n1. ROM 3's CLS_LOWER with ATTR_P set to BORDCR meanwhile; stream -3 ($FD, the lower screen)\nselected (ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT).\n2. With Z, a disk error: PROMPT_DISK_ERR, answered by C, R or I.\n3. With NZ: DERR_INSERT, the drive letter A, DERR_ANY_KEY, then any key (WAIT_KEY).\n4. PROMPT_DONE: ROM 3's CLS_LOWER, stream -2 ($FE, the upper screen) selected.\nEntry: Z: H = the error (0-9), L = the drive letter, D = the track, E = the sector.\nNZ: A = the drive letter, E = the value to return.\nExit: Z: A = 0 for C, 1 for R, 2 for I. NZ: A = E.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"HL, DE and AF kept"},
        "8614": {"comment":"ATTR_P kept"},
        "8618": {"comment":"ATTR_P = BORDCR: the lower screen's colours"},
        "8624": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLS_LOWER"},
        "8627": {"comment":"Stream -3: the lower screen"},
        "8629": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "8632": {"comment":"ATTR_P back"},
        "8636": {"comment":"AF and DE back; BC = the HL passed"},
        "8639": {"comment":"Z: a disk error"},
        "8641": {"comment":"NZ: \"Introduzca en la unidad \""},
        "8644": {"comment":"The drive letter kept"},
        "8645": {"comment":"Printed (PROMPT_TEXT)"},
        "8648": {"comment":"The drive letter back"},
        "8649": {"comment":"AT"},
        "8650": {"comment":"\" y luego pulse una tecla\""},
        "8653": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "8656": {"comment":"Any key (WAIT_KEY)"},
        "8659": {"synopsis":"Either way: ROM 3's CLS_LOWER, stream -2 ($FE, the upper screen) selected, A = E.\nExit: A = E.","comment":"E kept: the answer"},
        "8660": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLS_LOWER"},
        "8663": {"comment":"Stream -2: the upper screen"},
        "8665": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "8668": {"comment":"A = E"},
        "8671": {"synopsis":"Prints the text at HL through RST $10, up to and including the character with bit 7 set\n(printed without it).\nExit: HL on that last character.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"The character: bit 7 set?"},
        "8674": {"comment":"Its flags kept"},
        "8675": {"comment":"Printed without bit 7"},
        "8678": {"comment":"Bit 7 was set: done, HL on it"},
        "8680": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8681": {"comment":"Round again"},
        "8683": {"synopsis":"Z: a disk error. AT 0,0, \"UNIDAD \" (DERR_DRIVE_AT), the drive letter C and ':'; then\nmessage B of DERR_MSGS. When its first byte is 1 or 2, the track first (\" PISTA \" and D,\nPROMPT_TRACK), the byte passed over; with 2 also \" SECTOR \", E and ENTER (PROMPT_SECTOR).\nThe message in a contrasting INK (PROMPT_ERR_INK), DERR_QUESTION, and the answer\n(PROMPT_ANSWER).\nROM 2's sidecar records CAT with no disk asking \"UNIDAD A: PISTA 000 SECTOR 000\", \"SIN\nDATOS\" and the question.","comment":"AT 0,0, \"UNIDAD \""},
        "8686": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "8689": {"comment":"The drive letter (C)"},
        "8691": {"comment":"Then ':'"},
        "8694": {"comment":"BC = the error (B)"},
        "8697": {"comment":"HL = the error x 2"},
        "8700": {"comment":"+ DERR_MSGS"},
        "8704": {"comment":"HL = the error's message"},
        "8708": {"comment":"Its first byte below 3?"},
        "8711": {"comment":"No: the text alone"},
        "8713": {"comment":"\" PISTA \" and the track; HL one on"},
        "8716": {"comment":"2: the sector too?"},
        "8720": {"comment":"\" SECTOR \", the sector, ENTER"},
        "8723": {"synopsis":"The message at HL in an INK that shows on the paper: ATTR_T's INK made 5 when its PAPER is\n0-3, 2 when it is 4-7; ATTR_T put back after the message.","comment":"ATTR_T kept"},
        "8727": {"comment":"PAPER 4 or more?"},
        "8731": {"comment":"Yes: INK 2"},
        "8733": {"comment":"No: INK 5"},
        "8737": {"synopsis":"PAPER 4-7: INK 2.","comment":"INK 2"},
        "8739": {"synopsis":"ATTR_T with INK E, the message printed (PROMPT_TEXT), ATTR_T back; then DERR_QUESTION.","comment":"ATTR_T with INK E"},
        "8744": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "8747": {"comment":"The message printed"},
        "8750": {"comment":"ATTR_T back"},
        "8754": {"comment":"\"]REINTENTAR, IGNORAR O CANCELAR?\""},
        "8757": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "8760": {"synopsis":"A key (WAIT_KEY), in upper case: C gives E = 0, R 1, I 2, each on to PROMPT_DONE; any other\nkey is passed over.","comment":"A key (WAIT_KEY)"},
        "8763": {"comment":"Upper case"},
        "8765": {"comment":"E = 0: C (cancel)?"},
        "8769": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "8771": {"comment":"E = 1: R (retry)?"},
        "8774": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "8776": {"comment":"E = 2: I (ignore)?"},
        "8779": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "8781": {"comment":"Another key"},
        "8783": {"synopsis":"Prints \" PISTA \" (DERR_TRACK_TXT) and the track D in three digits (PROMPT_DECIMAL).\nExit: HL one on.\nKeeps AF, DE.","comment":"AF, DE and HL kept"},
        "8786": {"comment":"\" PISTA \""},
        "8789": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "8792": {"comment":"The track (D)"},
        "8793": {"comment":"In decimal"},
        "8796": {"comment":"HL, DE and AF back"},
        "8799": {"comment":"Past the message's first byte"},
        "8801": {"synopsis":"Prints \" SECTOR \" (DERR_SECTOR_TXT), the sector E in three digits (PROMPT_DECIMAL) and\nENTER.\nKeeps AF, DE, HL.","comment":"AF, DE and HL kept"},
        "8804": {"comment":"\" SECTOR \""},
        "8807": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "8810": {"comment":"The sector (E)"},
        "8811": {"comment":"In decimal"},
        "8814": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "8817": {"comment":"HL, DE and AF back"},
        "8821": {"synopsis":"Prints A (0-255) as three decimal digits, leading zeros kept: the hundreds, the tens and the\nunits, each counted in E and printed by PROMPT_DIGIT.\nChanges: AF, E.","comment":"E counts the hundreds"},
        "8823": {"synopsis":"One hundred taken off.","comment":"Another hundred?"},
        "8825": {"comment":"No: the rest"},
        "8827": {"comment":"Counted"},
        "8830": {"synopsis":"The hundreds digit printed; then the tens counted.","comment":"A = the rest"},
        "8832": {"comment":"The hundreds digit"},
        "8835": {"comment":"E counts the tens"},
        "8837": {"synopsis":"One ten taken off.","comment":"Another ten?"},
        "8839": {"comment":"No: the rest"},
        "8841": {"comment":"Counted"},
        "8844": {"synopsis":"The tens digit printed, then the units.","comment":"A = the units"},
        "8846": {"comment":"The tens digit"},
        "8849": {"comment":"The units digit"},
        "8853": {"synopsis":"Prints E as a digit ('0' + E).\nKeeps AF.","comment":"A kept"},
        "8854": {"comment":"'0' + E"},
        "8857": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "8858": {"comment":"A back"},
        "8860": {"synopsis":"PROMPT_DISK_ERR's messages, one word for each disk error 0-9: DERR_NOT_READY,\nDERR_WRITE_PROT, DERR_SEEK, DERR_DATA, DERR_NO_DATA, DERR_NO_MARK, DERR_FORMAT,\nDERR_UNKNOWN,\nDERR_CHANGED, DERR_UNSUITABLE. Each message starts with $0D (the text on a line of its\nown), 1 (the track printed first) or 2 (the track and sector first); its last character\nhas bit 7 set."},
        "8880": {"synopsis":"PROMPT_DISK_ERR's first text: AT 0,0, then \"UNIDAD \" ($22B3), the space with bit 7 set."},
        "8890": {"synopsis":"PROMPT_TRACK's text: \" PISTA \", the last space with bit 7 set."},
        "8897": {"synopsis":"PROMPT_SECTOR's text: \" SECTOR \", the last space with bit 7 set."},
        "8905": {"synopsis":"The question after a disk error: $5D, then \"REINTENTAR, IGNORAR O CANCELAR?\", the '?' with\nbit 7 set. In the Spanish ROM 3's character set $5D is drawn as an inverted question mark."},
        "8937": {"synopsis":"Disk error 0: ENTER, \"NO PREPARADA\", ENTER (with bit 7 set)."},
        "8951": {"synopsis":"Disk error 1: ENTER, \"DISCO PROTEGIDO CONTRA ESCRITURA\", the last 'A' with bit 7 set (no\nENTER after it)."},
        "8984": {"synopsis":"Disk error 2: 1 (the track first), ENTER, \"FALLO DE BUSQUEDA\", ENTER (with bit 7 set)."},
        "9004": {"synopsis":"Disk error 3: 2 (the track and sector first), \"ERROR DE DATOS\", ENTER (with bit 7 set)."},
        "9020": {"synopsis":"Disk error 4: 2 (the track and sector first), \"SIN DATOS\", ENTER (with bit 7 set)."},
        "9031": {"synopsis":"Disk error 5: 2 (the track and sector first), \"FALTA MARCA DE DIRECCIONES\", ENTER (with\nbit 7 set)."},
        "9059": {"synopsis":"Disk error 6: ENTER, \"FORMATO INCORRECTO\", ENTER (with bit 7 set)."},
        "9079": {"synopsis":"Disk error 7: 2 (the track and sector first), \"ERROR DESCONOCIDO\", ENTER (with bit 7 set)."},
        "9098": {"synopsis":"Disk error 8: ENTER, \"DISCO CAMBIADO; SUSTITUYALO\", ENTER (with bit 7 set)."},
        "9127": {"synopsis":"Disk error 9: ENTER, \"DISCO NO ADECUADO\", ENTER (with bit 7 set)."},
        "9146": {"synopsis":"PROMPT_KEY's text with NZ, before the drive letter: \"Introduzca en la unidad \", the last\nspace with bit 7 set."},
        "9183": {"synopsis":"PROMPT_KEY's text with NZ, after the drive letter: \" y luego pulse una tecla\", the last\n'a' with bit 7 set."},
        "9207": {"synopsis":"The start of a program that tests the machine's hardware; no call or jump in this ROM's\ncode reaches it. Each check shifts one bit into IX at bit 0 (TEST_RESULT_BIT), 1 for a pass:\n1. Interrupts off, IX = $FFFF, border white, SP = $7FFF; $2B17 first.\n2. The screen cleared, INK 7 and PAPER 0, the text at $3481, 40 frames waited.\n3. Border green and the RAM test: banks 0-7 filled with D = $00; each byte checked and\nmade its complement, banks 0 up; each checked and given D again, from $FFFF of bank 7\ndown; the same again with D = $FF. A byte that differs: RAM_FAIL.\n4. Then BANK_ID_TEST.","comment":"Interrupts off"},
        "9208": {"comment":"IX: the results, one bit per check"},
        "9212": {"comment":"Border white"},
        "9214": {"comment":"Border white"},
        "9216": {"comment":"The stack below $8000"},
        "9219": {"comment":"First $2B17"},
        "9222": {"comment":"Interrupts off, border white"},
        "9227": {"comment":"Screen cleared, plain colours (TEST_CLS)"},
        "9230": {"comment":"INK 7, PAPER 0"},
        "9236": {"comment":"The text at $3481"},
        "9242": {"comment":"40 frames (WAIT_40_FRAMES)"},
        "9245": {"comment":"Border green: the RAM test"},
        "9247": {"comment":"Border green"},
        "9249": {"comment":"Two passes; D = $00, the pattern"},
        "9252": {"synopsis":"One pass with pattern D: every bank filled with it.","comment":"Bank 0 first"},
        "9254": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "9257": {"synopsis":"Bank A filled with D, $C000-$FFFF.","comment":"Bank A paged in at $C000"},
        "9259": {"comment":"The bank number aside"},
        "9260": {"comment":"From $C000"},
        "9263": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"The pattern"},
        "9264": {"comment":"Up to $FFFF"},
        "9267": {"comment":"Up to $FFFF"},
        "9269": {"comment":"The next bank, up to 7"},
        "9273": {"comment":"All eight?"},
        "9275": {"comment":"Bank 0 again"},
        "9277": {"synopsis":"Bank A checked upwards: each byte must be D, then is made its complement.","comment":"Paged in"},
        "9279": {"comment":"The number aside"},
        "9280": {"comment":"From $C000"},
        "9283": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"Still the pattern? If not, RAM_FAIL"},
        "9285": {"comment":"No: RAM_FAIL"},
        "9287": {"comment":"Its complement written"},
        "9289": {"comment":"Up to $FFFF"},
        "9292": {"comment":"Up to $FFFF"},
        "9294": {"comment":"The next bank, up to 7"},
        "9298": {"comment":"All eight?"},
        "9300": {"comment":"From bank 7 down"},
        "9301": {"synopsis":"Bank A checked from the top down: each byte must be D's complement, then is D again.","comment":"The number aside; HL from $FFFF down"},
        "9305": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"Down one; below $C000?"},
        "9309": {"comment":"Yes: the next bank"},
        "9311": {"comment":"Still the complement? If not, RAM_FAIL"},
        "9314": {"comment":"No: RAM_FAIL"},
        "9316": {"comment":"The pattern again"},
        "9317": {"comment":"The next byte"},
        "9319": {"synopsis":"The next bank down.","comment":"Bank 0 done?"},
        "9322": {"comment":"Yes: the pass ends"},
        "9324": {"comment":"The bank below"},
        "9325": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9327": {"comment":"And checked"},
        "9329": {"synopsis":"The pass's end: a second one with D = $FF, then BANK_ID_TEST.","comment":"Both passes done? On to BANK_ID_TEST"},
        "9330": {"comment":"Both: BANK_ID_TEST"},
        "9333": {"comment":"The second pass with $FF"},
        "9335": {"comment":"Again"},
        "9338": {"synopsis":"A RAM byte did not hold its value: the start-up run again (TEST_REINIT), bank 0, INK 7 and\nPAPER 0, the screen cleared and \"RAM fail: address hhhh, page n\" printed, HL being the\naddress and A' the bank, in hex; then the machine stops (interrupts off and HALT).\nBANK_ID_FAIL comes here too, with HL = 0.","comment":"A = the bank"},
        "9339": {"comment":"Bank and address kept"},
        "9341": {"comment":"The start-up again (TEST_REINIT)"},
        "9344": {"comment":"Bank 0, paging byte 0"},
        "9351": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9353": {"comment":"INK 7, PAPER 0"},
        "9359": {"comment":"Screen cleared (TEST_CLS)"},
        "9362": {"comment":"'RAM fail: address '"},
        "9368": {"comment":"The address"},
        "9369": {"comment":"Its high byte in hex (TEST_HEX_A)"},
        "9370": {"comment":"Its high byte"},
        "9373": {"comment":"Its low byte"},
        "9377": {"comment":"The main registers aside"},
        "9378": {"comment":"', page '"},
        "9384": {"comment":"The bank, 0-7"},
        "9387": {"comment":"In hex"},
        "9391": {"comment":"Stopped for good"},
        "9392": {"comment":"For good"},
        "9393": {"synopsis":"Prints A as two hex digits (HEX_DIGITS, TEST_PRINT_A), the alternate DE and HL used for\nthe lookup.\nChanges: AF, B, the alternate DE and HL.","comment":"HL and A kept"},
        "9396": {"comment":"The high digit"},
        "9404": {"comment":"Two digits"},
        "9406": {"synopsis":"One digit.","comment":"DE = the digit (alternate set)"},
        "9410": {"comment":"Its character from HEX_DIGITS"},
        "9415": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "9418": {"comment":"Then the low digit"},
        "9422": {"comment":"Both?"},
        "9424": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "9425": {"comment":"Done"},
        "9426": {"synopsis":"RAM_FAIL's text: AT 10,0, \"RAM fail: address \", $FF at its end."},
        "9448": {"synopsis":"No call or jump in this ROM's code reaches it. Border black, the picture cleared, then for\never each attribute from $5800 to $5AFF made of three samples of the EAR input (port $FE\nbit 6) shifted into C.","comment":"Border black"},
        "9450": {"comment":"Border black"},
        "9452": {"comment":"The picture cleared, $4000-$57FF"},
        "9465": {"synopsis":"Again from $5800.","comment":"From the first attribute"},
        "9468": {"synopsis":"One attribute.","comment":"Three samples, C = 0"},
        "9471": {"synopsis":"One sample.","comment":"The EAR bit"},
        "9475": {"comment":"Into C, shifted on"},
        "9479": {"comment":"Timing"},
        "9483": {"comment":"Three?"},
        "9485": {"comment":"The attribute"},
        "9487": {"comment":"Past $5AFF?"},
        "9490": {"comment":"No: the next attribute"},
        "9492": {"comment":"For ever"},
        "9494": {"synopsis":"RAM_FAIL's \", page \", $FF at its end."},
        "9502": {"synopsis":"The 16 hex digits, \"0123456789ABCDEF\", for TEST_HEX_A."},
        "9518": {"synopsis":"PAGING_RESULT's text: AT 10,0, \"RAM test passed\", $FF at its end."},
        "9537": {"synopsis":"Checks that the eight banks are eight: each gets its number at $CAFE, banks 0 up; then from\n7 down each must still hold its own (BANK_ID_FAIL if not). Then each bank's number goes to\n$E000, PAGE_ROM_TEST is copied to $D000 in banks 7 and 3 (COPY_PAGE_TEST) and run there\nwith bank 3 paged in.","comment":"Bank 0 first; HL = $CAFE"},
        "9542": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "9545": {"synopsis":"Its number written.","comment":"Bank A paged in"},
        "9547": {"comment":"Its number at $CAFE"},
        "9548": {"comment":"The next, up to 7"},
        "9551": {"comment":"All eight?"},
        "9553": {"synopsis":"Bank A - 1 checked, from 7 down.","comment":"The bank below paged in"},
        "9554": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9556": {"comment":"Its number still there?"},
        "9557": {"comment":"No: BANK_ID_FAIL"},
        "9560": {"comment":"Bank 0 done?"},
        "9561": {"comment":"No: the next one down"},
        "9563": {"comment":"Interrupts off"},
        "9567": {"comment":"Bank 0 first"},
        "9569": {"synopsis":"Its number at $E000.","comment":"Bank A paged in"},
        "9571": {"comment":"Its number at $E000"},
        "9574": {"comment":"The next, up to 7"},
        "9577": {"comment":"All eight?"},
        "9579": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "9580": {"comment":"The ROM test copied into it"},
        "9583": {"comment":"And into bank 3"},
        "9588": {"comment":"Run there, bank 3 paged in"},
        "9591": {"synopsis":"Pages bank A in at $C000 and copies PAGE_ROM_TEST ($B9 bytes from $2588) to $D000 in it.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Bank A paged in"},
        "9594": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9596": {"comment":"PAGE_ROM_TEST to $D000, $B9 bytes"},
        "9607": {"comment":"Done"},
        "9608": {"synopsis":"Runs at $D000, copied there in banks 3 and 7 by COPY_PAGE_TEST (its calls of $D08E and\n$D09B are RESULT_BIT_RAM and ROM_SUM; SPECIAL_BANKS is read at $D0A9):\n1. The four all-RAM configurations of port $1FFD (1, 3, 5, 7): the bytes at $2000, $6000,\n$A000 and $E000, where BANK_ID_TEST put each bank's number, must give SPECIAL_BANKS;\nD = 1 when all do, 0 when one does not, kept in the alternate set.\n2. The ROMs summed (ROM_SUM): ROM 0 and ROM 1 together give one result bit; then with\n$1FFD = 4, two more sums give another.\n3. Normal paging back, ROM 0, the copies at $5B5C and $5B67 = 0, and on at PAGING_RESULT.","comment":"Configuration 0, all-RAM paging on"},
        "9610": {"comment":"DE = SPECIAL_BANKS (its copy at $D0A9)"},
        "9613": {"comment":"HL = $2000, in the first quarter"},
        "9616": {"synopsis":"One configuration of port $1FFD.","comment":"The configuration set (port $1FFD)"},
        "9619": {"comment":"All-RAM configuration A"},
        "9621": {"comment":"Kept aside"},
        "9622": {"comment":"BC = $4000: a quarter"},
        "9625": {"synopsis":"One quarter: its byte must be the bank number expected.","comment":"The bank expected here"},
        "9627": {"comment":"The number BANK_ID_TEST wrote?"},
        "9628": {"comment":"No: SPECIAL_FAIL"},
        "9630": {"comment":"The next quarter, up to $E000"},
        "9631": {"comment":"Until past $FFFF"},
        "9633": {"comment":"The next configuration: 3, 5, 7"},
        "9636": {"comment":"All four?"},
        "9638": {"comment":"No: the next configuration"},
        "9640": {"comment":"D = 1: all right"},
        "9642": {"comment":"On to the ROMs"},
        "9644": {"synopsis":"A wrong bank: D = 0.","comment":"D = 0: a wrong bank"},
        "9647": {"synopsis":"The ROM checksums.","comment":"D into the alternate set"},
        "9648": {"comment":"Bank 3 and ROM 0 ($7FFD = 3, $1FFD = 0)"},
        "9653": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9658": {"comment":"Normal paging, ROM 0"},
        "9660": {"comment":"ROM 0 sums to 0? (ROM_SUM)"},
        "9663": {"comment":"No: ROM_LOW_BAD"},
        "9665": {"comment":"ROM 1: $7FFD = $13"},
        "9670": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9672": {"comment":"Sums to 0?"},
        "9675": {"comment":"No: ROM_LOW_BAD"},
        "9677": {"comment":"Both: a 1 result bit"},
        "9678": {"comment":"Carry in (RESULT_BIT_RAM)"},
        "9681": {"synopsis":"The second pair of sums, $1FFD bit 2 set.","comment":"$1FFD = 4"},
        "9686": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9688": {"comment":"$7FFD = 3: ROM 2"},
        "9693": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9695": {"comment":"Sums to 0?"},
        "9698": {"comment":"No: ROM_HIGH_BAD"},
        "9700": {"comment":"$7FFD = $0B: still ROM 2 (bit 4 clear)"},
        "9705": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9707": {"comment":"Sums to 0?"},
        "9710": {"comment":"No: ROM_HIGH_BAD"},
        "9712": {"comment":"Both: a 1 result bit"},
        "9713": {"comment":"Carry in (RESULT_BIT_RAM)"},
        "9716": {"synopsis":"Normal paging again, ROM 0; the copies of both ports 0; on in ROM 0.","comment":"$7FFD = 3"},
        "9723": {"comment":"$1FFD = 0: ROM 0"},
        "9729": {"comment":"The copies at $5B5C and $5B67 = 0"},
        "9735": {"comment":"On in ROM 0"},
        "9738": {"synopsis":"ROM 0 or 1 did not sum to 0: a 0 bit; on to the second pair.","comment":"A 0 result bit"},
        "9739": {"comment":"No carry in (RESULT_BIT_RAM)"},
        "9742": {"comment":"The second pair"},
        "9744": {"synopsis":"The second pair failed: a 0 bit.","comment":"A 0 result bit"},
        "9745": {"comment":"No carry in (RESULT_BIT_RAM)"},
        "9748": {"comment":"Normal paging again"},
        "9750": {"synopsis":"PAGE_ROM_TEST's copy of TEST_RESULT_BIT (at $D08E): the carry shifted into IX at bit 0.\nKeeps DE.","comment":"DE kept"},
        "9751": {"comment":"DE = IX"},
        "9754": {"comment":"Carry in at bit 0, the rest up one"},
        "9758": {"comment":"IX = it"},
        "9762": {"comment":"Done"},
        "9763": {"synopsis":"Runs at $D09B: adds up the 16K at $0000-$3FFF, the ROM paged in, in A (modulo 256).\nExit: Z when the sum is 0.\nChanges: A, D, HL.","comment":"A = 0, HL = 0"},
        "9766": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"Added"},
        "9768": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "9769": {"comment":"Up to $3FFF?"},
        "9773": {"comment":"No: the next byte"},
        "9775": {"comment":"Z when 0"},
        "9777": {"synopsis":"The banks PAGE_ROM_TEST expects at $0000, $4000, $8000 and $C000 in the four all-RAM\nconfigurations: 0 1 2 3, 4 5 6 7, 4 5 6 3, 4 7 6 3 (read at $D0A9)."},
        "9793": {"synopsis":"Shifts the carry into IX at bit 0, the rest up one: each check's result, carry for a pass.\nKeeps DE.","comment":"DE kept"},
        "9794": {"comment":"DE = IX"},
        "9797": {"comment":"Carry in at bit 0, the rest up one"},
        "9801": {"comment":"IX = it"},
        "9806": {"synopsis":"Back in ROM 0 after PAGE_ROM_TEST: bank 0, SP = $7FFF, the configurations' result (D = 1) as\na\nbit; the start-up run again, \"RAM test passed\" shown for 40 frames; then TEST_SEQUENCE.","comment":"Bank 0, ROM 0"},
        "9811": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9813": {"comment":"The stack again"},
        "9816": {"comment":"D = the configurations' result"},
        "9817": {"comment":"Carry when D is 1"},
        "9819": {"comment":"The result bit"},
        "9822": {"comment":"The start-up again (TEST_REINIT)"},
        "9825": {"comment":"Screen cleared"},
        "9828": {"comment":"'RAM test passed'"},
        "9834": {"comment":"40 frames"},
        "9837": {"comment":"The other tests"},
        "9839": {"synopsis":"A bank did not hold its number: the start-up run again (TEST_REINIT), then RAM_FAIL with\nHL = 0.","comment":"The start-up again (TEST_REINIT)"},
        "9842": {"comment":"AF swapped, as RAM_FAIL swaps it back"},
        "9843": {"comment":"Address 0"},
        "9846": {"comment":"Reported (RAM_FAIL)"},
        "9849": {"synopsis":"The other tests in turn: $2EB9, $2AD6, $2B7D, KEYBOARD_TEST, $2E3F, $2E8E, $2BF0, $2D44,\n$2C6B, PRINTER_TEST, $3778 and $37C3, then on at $2DB1.","comment":"Each test in turn"},
        "9852": {"comment":"$2AD6"},
        "9855": {"comment":"$2B7D"},
        "9858": {"comment":"The keys (KEYBOARD_TEST)"},
        "9861": {"comment":"$2E3F"},
        "9864": {"comment":"$2E8E"},
        "9867": {"comment":"$2BF0"},
        "9870": {"comment":"$2D44"},
        "9873": {"comment":"$2C6B"},
        "9876": {"comment":"The printer (PRINTER_TEST)"},
        "9879": {"comment":"$3778"},
        "9882": {"comment":"$37C3"},
        "9885": {"comment":"Then $2DB1"},
        "9888": {"synopsis":"Tests the printer port:\n1. BUSY: with the printer turned off line (a key waited for), bit 0 of port $0FFD must be\n1; turned on line, 0. One result bit.\n2. Data: bit 4 set in $5B67 (the strobe's resting level); characters $20-$7F and $A0-$FF\nsent twice (PRN_COUNTED, an ENTER after each 72), Q stopping it; then ENTER (a pass) or\nSPACE asked for: another bit.","comment":"Screen cleared"},
        "9891": {"comment":"'Printer BUSY signal test'"},
        "9897": {"comment":"'Turn the printer '"},
        "9903": {"comment":"'OFFLINE'"},
        "9909": {"synopsis":"PRINTER_TEST's \"Press any key to continue\" and the key. The JP at $010C names this address\ntoo, but it runs with ROM 1 paged in, so nothing in this ROM jumps here.","comment":"'Press any key to continue'"},
        "9915": {"comment":"A key (WAIT_NEW_KEY)"},
        "9918": {"comment":"Port $0FFD: BUSY in bit 0"},
        "9923": {"comment":"Busy while off line? If not, a fail"},
        "9925": {"comment":"Not busy: BUSY_FAIL"},
        "9927": {"comment":"'ONLINE ' over it"},
        "9933": {"comment":"A key"},
        "9936": {"comment":"Port $0FFD again"},
        "9941": {"comment":"Not busy now?"},
        "9943": {"comment":"Busy: BUSY_FAIL"},
        "9945": {"comment":"Carry: a pass"},
        "9948": {"synopsis":"BUSY wrong: no carry.","comment":"No carry: a fail"},
        "9950": {"synopsis":"The BUSY result into IX; then the data test.","comment":"The result bit"},
        "9953": {"comment":"Screen cleared"},
        "9956": {"comment":"Strobe bit 4 set in the $1FFD copy"},
        "9961": {"comment":"'Printer data test'"},
        "9967": {"comment":"The instructions, two lines"},
        "9973": {"comment":"E = 0: the column"},
        "9975": {"comment":"Two passes"},
        "9977": {"synopsis":"The next pass.","comment":"Both done? The question"},
        "9978": {"comment":"Yes: PRN_ASK_OK"},
        "9980": {"comment":"From a space"},
        "9982": {"synopsis":"One character.","comment":"Count and character kept"},
        "9984": {"comment":"Sent (PRN_COUNTED)"},
        "9989": {"comment":"The next; past $7F?"},
        "9992": {"comment":"Yes: on from $A0"},
        "9994": {"comment":"Past $FF (0)? The next pass"},
        "9995": {"comment":"Yes: the next pass"},
        "9997": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "9999": {"synopsis":"$80-$9F skipped.","comment":"From $A0"},
        "10001": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "10003": {"synopsis":"Sends A to the printer (PRN_SEND) and counts it in E; after 72 an ENTER too, E = 0.\nKeeps A.","comment":"Sent (PRN_SEND)"},
        "10007": {"comment":"One more in the line"},
        "10008": {"comment":"72?"},
        "10011": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "10013": {"comment":"E = 0; an ENTER sent"},
        "10020": {"synopsis":"A back.","comment":"A back"},
        "10022": {"synopsis":"Sends A to the printer: waits while bit 0 of port $0FFD (BUSY) is 1, Q giving up (PRN_QUIT);\nA out to port $0FFD; then a strobe pulse on port $1FFD bit 4, from the copy at $5B67\n(cleared, then set again), with interrupts off.\nChanges: A, BC.","comment":"A kept"},
        "10023": {"synopsis":"Waiting while the printer is busy.","comment":"Q down? Then the printing stops"},
        "10025": {"comment":"Half-row $FBFE"},
        "10028": {"comment":"Q down: PRN_QUIT"},
        "10030": {"comment":"BUSY?"},
        "10033": {"comment":"Port $0FFD"},
        "10037": {"comment":"Busy: wait"},
        "10039": {"comment":"The byte out to port $0FFD"},
        "10042": {"comment":"Interrupts off for the pulse"},
        "10043": {"comment":"A = the $1FFD copy, strobe bit set"},
        "10046": {"synopsis":"The strobe bit toggled out: low, then high again.","comment":"Strobe bit toggled out"},
        "10051": {"comment":"Out to port $1FFD"},
        "10053": {"comment":"Low now? Then back high"},
        "10057": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "10058": {"comment":"Done"},
        "10059": {"synopsis":"Q stops the printing: five words dropped (PRN_SEND's AF and return, PRN_COUNTED's return,\nthe loop's AF and BC), then PRN_ASK_OK.","comment":"Five words off the stack"},
        "10064": {"synopsis":"Asks whether the characters printed well: ENTER (carry) or SPACE (TEST_ENTER_SPACE); the\nanswer is the result bit.","comment":"'If characters printed OK, ...'"},
        "10070": {"comment":"ENTER: carry; SPACE: none"},
        "10073": {"comment":"The result bit"},
        "10076": {"comment":"Done"},
        "10077": {"synopsis":"Waits for a key: FLAGS bit 5 cleared, waited for until the interrupt sets it, cleared again.\nChanges: HL.","comment":"FLAGS"},
        "10080": {"comment":"No new key"},
        "10082": {"synopsis":"Until bit 5 is set.","comment":"A key yet?"},
        "10084": {"comment":"No: wait"},
        "10086": {"comment":"Taken"},
        "10088": {"comment":"Done"},
        "10089": {"synopsis":"AT 4,4, \"Printer data test\", $FF at its end."},
        "10110": {"synopsis":"AT 8,1, \"Make sure printer is ready\", AT 10,1, \"Press Q to quit printing\", $FF."},
        "10167": {"synopsis":"AT 12,1, \"If characters printed OK,\", ENTER, \"Press [ENTER], otherwise [SPACE]\",\n$FF at its end."},
        "10229": {"synopsis":"OVER 0, AT 4,4, \"Printer BUSY signal test\", $FF at its end."},
        "10259": {"synopsis":"AT 8,8, \"Turn the printer \", $FF at its end."},
        "10280": {"synopsis":"AT 10,12, \"ONLINE \", $FF at its end."},
        "10291": {"synopsis":"AT 10,12, \"OFFLINE\", $FF at its end."},
        "10302": {"synopsis":"AT 12,4, \"Press any key to continue\", $FF at its end."},
        "10331": {"synopsis":"AT 16,5, \"Passed - press [ENTER]\", $FF at its end. No LD in this ROM's code points at it."},
        "10357": {"synopsis":"AT 16,5, \"Failed - press [SPACE]\", $FF at its end. No LD in this ROM's code points at it."},
        "10383": {"synopsis":"Runs the start-up again from $016C (the routines at $5B00, the system variables and so on)\nwith A' = 'R' ($52), which makes it end at TEST_RESTARTED instead; the stack is kept, as the\nstart-up from $016C does not set SP, so the RET there comes back to this routine's caller.\nChanges: all registers.","comment":"'R': back by TEST_RESTARTED"},
        "10386": {"comment":"The start-up from $016C"},
        "10389": {"synopsis":"Where the start-up goes on when A' is 'R' (from $0261): stream 2 selected (ROM 3's\nSTREAM_SELECT), then COLOUR_RESET, whose RET goes back to TEST_REINIT's caller.","comment":"Stream 2: the upper screen"},
        "10391": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "10394": {"synopsis":"Prints COLOUR_RESET_SEQ: INK 0, PAPER 7, BRIGHT, INVERSE, OVER and FLASH 0.","comment":"INK 0, PAPER 7, the rest 0"},
        "10397": {"comment":"Printed (TEST_PRINT_TEXT)"},
        "10401": {"synopsis":"COLOUR_RESET's codes: INK 0, PAPER 7, BRIGHT 0, INVERSE 0, OVER 0, FLASH 0, then $FF."},
        "10414": {"synopsis":"Waits 25 frames (HALT with interrupts on), then interrupts off. No call or jump in this\nROM's code reaches it.\nKeeps BC, HL.","comment":"BC and HL kept"},
        "10416": {"comment":"25 frames"},
        "10418": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "10419": {"synopsis":"One frame.","comment":"One frame"},
        "10420": {"comment":"25 of them"},
        "10424": {"comment":"Interrupts off"},
        "10426": {"synopsis":"Waits 40 frames (HALT with interrupts on), then interrupts off. Changes: B.","comment":"40 frames"},
        "10428": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "10429": {"synopsis":"One frame.","comment":"One frame"},
        "10430": {"comment":"40 of them"},
        "10432": {"comment":"Interrupts off"},
        "10434": {"synopsis":"A delay: HL counted down from $3000.\nChanges: A, HL.","comment":"$3000 rounds"},
        "10437": {"synopsis":"One round.","comment":"One round"},
        "10438": {"comment":"Time spent"},
        "10442": {"comment":"Zero?"},
        "10444": {"comment":"No: again"},
        "10447": {"synopsis":"Waits until no key is down, then for ENTER or SPACE (TEST_KEY_WAIT), then beeps\n(TEST_BEEP).\nExit: carry for ENTER, no carry for SPACE; interrupts off.\nKeeps BC, DE, HL.","comment":"HL, DE and BC kept"},
        "10450": {"comment":"All half-rows (port $00FE)"},
        "10453": {"synopsis":"Until every key is up.","comment":"No key down?"},
        "10459": {"comment":"Not yet: again"},
        "10461": {"synopsis":"Until ENTER or SPACE.","comment":"A key (TEST_KEY_WAIT)"},
        "10464": {"comment":"ENTER ($21)? Carry"},
        "10467": {"comment":"ENTER: done"},
        "10469": {"comment":"SPACE ($20)?"},
        "10471": {"comment":"Neither: another key"},
        "10473": {"synopsis":"The answer's flags kept over a beep.","comment":"Flags kept; a beep (TEST_BEEP)"},
        "10474": {"comment":"The beep (TEST_BEEP)"},
        "10482": {"synopsis":"Waits for a key: TEST_KEY_SCAN.","comment":"Scanned until a key is down"},
        "10486": {"synopsis":"Scans the keyboard until a key is down. Each key gets a number from its half-row and bit:\nhalf-row $FEFE gives $27, $1F, $17, $0F, $07 for bits 0-4 and each later half-row one less\n($BFFE bit 0, ENTER, is $21; $7FFE gives SPACE $20, SYMBOL SHIFT $18). A third key starts\nthe scan again.\nExit: A = E = the last key found; D = the one before, $FF when only one.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"L = $2F: the first half-row's number"},
        "10488": {"comment":"No key yet: D and E = $FF"},
        "10491": {"comment":"Half-row $FEFE first"},
        "10494": {"synopsis":"One half-row.","comment":"Keys down in it?"},
        "10499": {"comment":"None: the next half-row"},
        "10501": {"comment":"H = them"},
        "10502": {"comment":"A = the half-row's number"},
        "10503": {"synopsis":"A key found: a third one starts again.","comment":"A third key? Then again from the start"},
        "10504": {"comment":"Yes: again from the start"},
        "10506": {"synopsis":"The key's bit found, its number worked out.","comment":"Less 8 for each bit"},
        "10508": {"comment":"This bit?"},
        "10510": {"comment":"Not this bit: the next"},
        "10512": {"comment":"D = the key before, E = this one"},
        "10514": {"comment":"More keys in the half-row?"},
        "10516": {"synopsis":"The next half-row, up to $7FFE.","comment":"The next half-row's number"},
        "10517": {"comment":"The next half-row; all eight?"},
        "10519": {"comment":"Not the last: again"},
        "10521": {"comment":"A key found? A = it"},
        "10524": {"comment":"Yes: back"},
        "10525": {"comment":"None? Scan again"},
        "10531": {"synopsis":"Prints the bytes at HL up to an $FF (RST $10).\nExit: HL at the $FF.\nChanges: A.","comment":"The end?"},
        "10534": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "10535": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "10536": {"comment":"The next"},
        "10537": {"comment":"Again"},
        "10539": {"synopsis":"Prints INK B and PAPER C.\nChanges: A.","comment":"INK B"},
        "10541": {"comment":"INK"},
        "10543": {"comment":"Colour B"},
        "10544": {"comment":"PAPER C"},
        "10546": {"comment":"PAPER"},
        "10548": {"comment":"Colour C"},
        "10550": {"synopsis":"Prints A (ROM 3's PRINT_A at $0010).","comment":"Printed (ROM 3's PRINT_A)"},
        "10554": {"synopsis":"Clears the screen (ROM 3's CLEAR_SCREEN) and prints COLOUR_RESET_SEQ.","comment":"Screen cleared (ROM 3's CLEAR_SCREEN)"},
        "10557": {"comment":"Plain colours (COLOUR_RESET)"},
        "10560": {"synopsis":"A short beep: the tone routine at $3709 with HL = $0100 and DE = $00A0; interrupts\noff after it.","comment":"The tone's HL and DE"},
        "10566": {"synopsis":"The tone at $3709 with HL and DE as given (from $2A2D and $2EA6); interrupts off after it.","comment":"The tone ($3709)"},
        "10569": {"comment":"Interrupts off"},
        "10571": {"synopsis":"Carry when SPACE is up (port $7FFE bit 0). No call or jump in this ROM's code reaches it.\nChanges: A.","comment":"Half-row $7FFE"},
        "10575": {"comment":"Carry: SPACE up"},
        "10577": {"synopsis":"As SPACE_UP, through RR A (from $2C18).\nChanges: A.","comment":"Half-row $7FFE"},
        "10581": {"comment":"Carry: SPACE up"},
        "10584": {"synopsis":"Z when, in half-row $7FFE, SPACE and SYMBOL SHIFT are down and M, N and B up. No call or\njump in this ROM's code reaches it.\nChanges: A.","comment":"Half-row $7FFE"},
        "10588": {"comment":"Bits 0 and 1 down, 2-4 up?"},
        "10593": {"synopsis":"Prints D spaces; A' = $38. No call or jump in this ROM's code reaches it.\nExit: D = 0.","comment":"A' = $38"},
        "10596": {"synopsis":"One space.","comment":"A space"},
        "10598": {"comment":"Printed (TEST_PRINT_A)"},
        "10601": {"comment":"D of them"},
        "10602": {"comment":"Until D is 0"},
        "10605": {"synopsis":"Tests the keys: screen cleared, BORDCR = $38, border white, the text at $3137 printed, a\ndelay (TEST_DELAY), then KEY_TEST_KEYS.","comment":"Screen cleared"},
        "10608": {"comment":"BORDCR: paper white, ink black"},
        "10613": {"comment":"Border white"},
        "10615": {"comment":"Border white"},
        "10617": {"comment":"The text at $3137"},
        "10623": {"comment":"A delay (TEST_DELAY)"},
        "10626": {"comment":"The keys (KEY_TEST_KEYS)"},
        "10630": {"synopsis":"Asks for the keys listed at $2A61 in turn ($FF at its end): each a key number as\nTEST_KEY_SCAN gives it, or a code for a pair of keys (KEY_CAPS_PAIR, KEY_SYM_PAIR). Any\nother\nkey or pair is passed over; the code in E goes on to the comparison at $2A19.","comment":"The list of keys expected"},
        "10634": {"synopsis":"The next key expected.","comment":"The list's place"},
        "10635": {"comment":"A = the key expected"},
        "10636": {"comment":"The end ($FF)?"},
        "10637": {"comment":"The list done"},
        "10638": {"comment":"The place kept"},
        "10639": {"comment":"A key (TEST_KEY_WAIT)"},
        "10642": {"comment":"A pause of $1000 rounds"},
        "10645": {"synopsis":"The pause.","comment":"Down to 0"},
        "10648": {"comment":"Not yet"},
        "10650": {"comment":"One key only?"},
        "10653": {"comment":"Single: KEY_CODE_READY"},
        "10655": {"comment":"CAPS SHIFT ($27) and another?"},
        "10657": {"comment":"Yes: KEY_CAPS_PAIR"},
        "10659": {"comment":"SYMBOL SHIFT ($18) first?"},
        "10661": {"comment":"Yes: KEY_SYM_PAIR"},
        "10663": {"comment":"D and E swapped: SYMBOL SHIFT last?"},
        "10668": {"comment":"Yes: KEY_SYM_PAIR"},
        "10670": {"comment":"Another pair: passed over"},
        "10672": {"synopsis":"CAPS SHIFT and E's key: 0 gives $28, 1 $29, 2 $2A, 3 $2B, 4 $2C, 5 $2D, 6 $2E, 7 $2F, 8 $30,\n9 $31, SPACE $32, SYMBOL SHIFT $37; any other is passed over.","comment":"E = the other key: 0?"},
        "10679": {"comment":"1?"},
        "10685": {"comment":"2?"},
        "10691": {"comment":"3?"},
        "10697": {"comment":"4?"},
        "10703": {"comment":"5?"},
        "10709": {"comment":"6?"},
        "10715": {"comment":"7?"},
        "10721": {"comment":"8?"},
        "10727": {"comment":"9?"},
        "10733": {"comment":"SPACE?"},
        "10739": {"comment":"SYMBOL SHIFT?"},
        "10745": {"comment":"Any other: passed over"},
        "10747": {"synopsis":"SYMBOL SHIFT and E's key: M gives $33, N $34, O $35, P $36; any other is passed over.","comment":"E = the other key: M?"},
        "10752": {"synopsis":"The code in E (a single key comes here with Z set): on to the comparison at $2A19.","comment":"Matched: to the comparison"},
        "10754": {"comment":"N?"},
        "10760": {"comment":"O?"},
        "10766": {"comment":"P?"},
        "10772": {"comment":"Not one of them: wait again"},
        "10774": {"comment":"Always taken: NZ from the CP"},
        "10777": {"synopsis":"The keyboard test's check of one key (from the combining at $29B0-$2A12): code E against the\nexpected one at HL, which is kept on the stack.\n1. Different: back to the wait at $298A for\nthe same key.\n2. The same: the next entry stacked in its place; a short tone (TONE_OUT\nthrough $2946, HL = DE = $0080).\n3. The key's square in the picture painted red: its place\nfrom KEY_TEST_PLACES, $3B bytes on, gives the row (high nibble x 2 + 5) and the column (low\nnibble x 2 + 1), and a space is printed there with PAPER 2.\n4. On to the next key at $298A.","comment":"The code"},
        "10778": {"comment":"Expected one at HL, still stacked"},
        "10780": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "10781": {"comment":"No: wait again"},
        "10784": {"comment":"Next entry stacked instead"},
        "10787": {"comment":"A short tone: HL = DE = $0080"},
        "10793": {"comment":"Registers kept around it"},
        "10797": {"comment":"TONE_OUT, then DI"},
        "10800": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "10804": {"comment":"HL = the next entry, still stacked"},
        "10806": {"comment":"PAPER 2: red"},
        "10809": {"comment":"Colour 2"},
        "10812": {"comment":"Back to the matched entry"},
        "10813": {"comment":"Its place, $3B bytes on"},
        "10817": {"comment":"High nibble x 2"},
        "10820": {"comment":"Down three bits: the nibble x 2"},
        "10823": {"comment":"B = that + 6"},
        "10827": {"comment":"Low nibble x 2 + 1"},
        "10828": {"comment":"Low nibble only"},
        "10831": {"comment":"+ 1"},
        "10834": {"comment":"C = the column"},
        "10835": {"comment":"AT B - 1, C"},
        "10838": {"comment":"Row B - 1"},
        "10841": {"comment":"Column C"},
        "10843": {"comment":"A red space over the key"},
        "10846": {"comment":"Next key"},
        "10849": {"synopsis":"The keyboard test's keys in the order the picture (KEY_TEST_PIC) shows them, row by row:\n58 key codes as the scan at $28F6 numbers them ($27 CAPS SHIFT, $18 SYMBOL SHIFT, $26 A,\n$21 ENTER, $20 SPACE, ...), with $28-$32 and $37 for a key pressed with CAPS SHIFT and\n$33-$37 for one with SYMBOL SHIFT, as $29B0-$2A19 combine them. CAPS SHIFT and SYMBOL SHIFT\nare each in it twice. $FF ends it. Read at $298B and $2A1A."},
        "10908": {"synopsis":"Where each key of KEY_TEST_CODES is drawn, one byte per key at the same index ($3B bytes\non): the high nibble gives the row (x 2 + 5), the low one the column (x 2 + 1). Read at\n$2A41."},
        "10966": {"synopsis":"The SYMBOL SHIFT and A test: the screen cleared ($293A), border cyan, INK 6 and PAPER 0\n($292B), the instructions (SYMA_TEST_MSG); then the wait until SYMBOL SHIFT and A are both\ndown (SYMA_HELD), and $0200 more scans that must all find them still down.\nExit: through $2641, the result into IX: carry when they were held throughout.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "10969": {"comment":"Border 5: cyan"},
        "10973": {"comment":"INK 6, PAPER 0"},
        "10979": {"comment":"Title and instructions"},
        "10985": {"synopsis":"Waits until both keys are down.","comment":"SYMBOL SHIFT and A down?"},
        "10988": {"comment":"Not yet: again"},
        "10990": {"comment":"$0200 scans with both held"},
        "10993": {"synopsis":"One more scan with both held.","comment":"Count kept round the scan"},
        "10994": {"comment":"Still both down?"},
        "10998": {"comment":"Let go: failed"},
        "11000": {"comment":"Count down"},
        "11003": {"comment":"More to go"},
        "11005": {"comment":"Held throughout: passed"},
        "11006": {"comment":"Result into IX"},
        "11009": {"synopsis":"Let go too soon: no carry.","comment":"Failed: no carry"},
        "11013": {"synopsis":"Whether the keys down are SYMBOL SHIFT ($18) and A ($26), in either order, by the scan at\n$28F2.\nExit: Z when they are.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"D, E = the keys down"},
        "11016": {"comment":"The first SYMBOL SHIFT?"},
        "11021": {"comment":"No: the two swapped"},
        "11024": {"comment":"The other SYMBOL SHIFT?"},
        "11026": {"comment":"Neither: NZ"},
        "11027": {"synopsis":"SYMBOL SHIFT found: is the other key A?","comment":"Then the other A?"},
        "11030": {"comment":"Z when it is"},
        "11031": {"synopsis":"The test program's first test (from $2403): $288F (on through the start-up code at $016C),\nthe colour bars and a tone (COLOUR_BARS), the title, the instructions and the warning\n(TITLE_MSG), the answer read ($28CF: ENTER passes, SPACE fails) and recorded in IX ($2641);\nthen the sound chip's mixer (register 7) set to $FF, all off.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Start-up's set-up at $016C, A' = $52"},
        "11034": {"comment":"Colour bars and a tone"},
        "11037": {"comment":"BC = 0 (not read by the printer)"},
        "11040": {"comment":"Title, instructions, warning"},
        "11046": {"comment":"ENTER (carry) or SPACE"},
        "11049": {"comment":"Result into IX"},
        "11052": {"comment":"AY: C = $FD; B = $FF selects, $BF writes"},
        "11058": {"comment":"Register 7 (mixer) = $FF: all off"},
        "11060": {"comment":"Register 7 selected"},
        "11065": {"comment":"$FF written"},
        "11069": {"synopsis":"The colour test's picture and tone: the top attribute row gets 16 pairs of cells with\nattribute 0, 8, 16 ... 120 (PAPER 0-7, then the same with BRIGHT 1) and is copied down the\nwhole screen; the sound chip's registers are set from AY_SETTINGS; the mixer (register 7) =\n$FB, the tone on channel C only.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Attribute 0 first"},
        "11070": {"comment":"Top attribute row"},
        "11073": {"comment":"16 pairs"},
        "11075": {"synopsis":"One pair of cells.","comment":"Two cells alike"},
        "11078": {"comment":"Next paper colour; BRIGHT from the 9th"},
        "11081": {"comment":"Next pair"},
        "11083": {"comment":"The row copied down the screen"},
        "11086": {"comment":"The other 23 rows"},
        "11091": {"comment":"AY: C = $FD; B = $FF selects, $BF writes"},
        "11097": {"comment":"Register/value pairs"},
        "11100": {"synopsis":"One register/value pair, until a byte with bit 7 set.","comment":"Register number"},
        "11102": {"comment":"The end marker?"},
        "11104": {"comment":"Yes: the mixer next"},
        "11106": {"comment":"Selected"},
        "11109": {"comment":"Its value"},
        "11111": {"comment":"Written"},
        "11114": {"comment":"Next pair"},
        "11116": {"synopsis":"The mixer: tone C only.","comment":"AY ports again"},
        "11122": {"comment":"$FB: only channel C's tone on"},
        "11124": {"comment":"Register 7 selected"},
        "11129": {"comment":"Written"},
        "11133": {"synopsis":"The ULA test: the screen cleared, the title (ULA_TEST_MSG); OUT_LOOP copied to $6000 and\nrun there, in contended RAM; then, when a byte at $8000 keeps $AA, copied to $8000 and run\nthere too; border yellow. It always passes.\nExit: through $2641, carry into IX.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "11136": {"comment":"ULA TEST title"},
        "11142": {"comment":"OUT_LOOP to $6000"},
        "11148": {"comment":"Run in contended RAM"},
        "11151": {"comment":"Does $8000 keep a byte?"},
        "11156": {"comment":"Read back"},
        "11159": {"comment":"Kept?"},
        "11161": {"comment":"No: skip"},
        "11163": {"comment":"OUT_LOOP to $8000 too"},
        "11169": {"comment":"Run in uncontended RAM"},
        "11172": {"synopsis":"Border yellow; passed.","comment":"Border 6: yellow"},
        "11176": {"comment":"Always passed"},
        "11177": {"comment":"Result into IX"},
        "11180": {"synopsis":"Copies OUT_LOOP's $3B bytes to DE.\nEntry: DE = the place.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"From OUT_LOOP"},
        "11183": {"comment":"$3B bytes"},
        "11189": {"synopsis":"Copied to $6000 and $8000 by ULA_TEST and run there: $2000 rounds of 16 writes to port\n$FE, A flipping between $00 and $FF (border black and white, the MIC and speaker bits\ntoggling). Its only jump is relative, so it runs anywhere.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"$2000 rounds"},
        "11192": {"synopsis":"One round of 16 writes.","comment":"Border 0 first"},
        "11196": {"comment":"Flipped between the writes"},
        "11242": {"comment":"Count down"},
        "11245": {"comment":"More rounds"},
        "11247": {"comment":"Done"},
        "11248": {"synopsis":"The joystick test: the screen cleared and the instructions and picture (JOY_TEST_MSG); then\nscan after scan of the keyboard rows the joysticks read as, $EFFE (joystick 1, kept in D)\nand $F7FE (joystick 2, in E): each direction seen clears its bit, and when the bits change\nevery label seen so far is painted out (JOY_WIPE). All ten seen: passed; SPACE gives up:\nfailed.\nExit: through $2641, the result into IX: carry when all ten were seen.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "11251": {"comment":"Instructions and picture"},
        "11257": {"comment":"Five directions each, all unseen"},
        "11260": {"synopsis":"One scan of both joysticks.","comment":"The state kept for the next scan"},
        "11261": {"comment":"Row $EFFE: joystick 1"},
        "11264": {"comment":"Bits 0-4: 0 when pressed"},
        "11266": {"comment":"Pressed bits as 1s"},
        "11267": {"comment":"Cleared from D"},
        "11269": {"comment":"D = what is still unseen"},
        "11270": {"comment":"Row $F7FE: joystick 2"},
        "11273": {"comment":"Bits 0-4: 0 when pressed"},
        "11275": {"comment":"Pressed bits as 1s"},
        "11276": {"comment":"Cleared from E"},
        "11278": {"comment":"E = what is still unseen"},
        "11279": {"comment":"BC = the last state"},
        "11280": {"comment":"Joystick 1 changed?"},
        "11284": {"comment":"Joystick 2 changed?"},
        "11288": {"comment":"SPACE pressed? (carry: no)"},
        "11291": {"comment":"Not pressed: again"},
        "11293": {"comment":"A zero byte read: again"},
        "11295": {"comment":"Given up: failed"},
        "11296": {"comment":"To the record"},
        "11298": {"synopsis":"Every direction seen: carry.","comment":"All seen: passed"},
        "11299": {"synopsis":"The result into IX.","comment":"Result into IX"},
        "11302": {"synopsis":"The bits changed: the label of every direction seen so far painted out, joystick 1's\nfrom D's bits 0-4, then joystick 2's from E's, with their places from JOY_PLACES.","comment":"New state kept"},
        "11303": {"comment":"Joystick 1's label places"},
        "11306": {"comment":"Five directions"},
        "11308": {"synopsis":"One direction of joystick 1.","comment":"Next bit: seen?"},
        "11310": {"comment":"Seen: its label painted out"},
        "11313": {"comment":"Next place"},
        "11315": {"comment":"Next of five"},
        "11317": {"comment":"Joystick 2's five"},
        "11319": {"synopsis":"One direction of joystick 2.","comment":"Next bit: seen?"},
        "11321": {"comment":"Seen: its label painted out"},
        "11324": {"comment":"Next place"},
        "11326": {"comment":"Next of five"},
        "11328": {"comment":"State back"},
        "11329": {"comment":"Everything seen?"},
        "11331": {"comment":"Yes: passed"},
        "11333": {"comment":"Not yet: again"},
        "11336": {"synopsis":"Paints one label out: two spaces with PAPER 2 at the place HL points to (a row, 3 below\nthe screen row, then a column), then PAPER 7.\nEntry: HL = the place's row byte.\nExit: HL as it came.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"Counter kept"},
        "11337": {"comment":"B = row, C = column"},
        "11340": {"comment":"AT B - 3, C"},
        "11343": {"comment":"Row - 3"},
        "11348": {"comment":"Column"},
        "11350": {"comment":"PAPER 2: red"},
        "11356": {"comment":"Two red spaces"},
        "11359": {"comment":"Second space"},
        "11362": {"comment":"PAPER 7"},
        "11368": {"comment":"HL back to the row byte"},
        "11369": {"comment":"Counter back"},
        "11371": {"synopsis":"The second screen test: with interrupts off, the attributes all 0 (black on black); the\ntitle and 'Passed - press [ENTER]' printed; RAM bank 7 paged in at $C000 and the screen\ncopied to its screen ($C000-$D7FF); the title and 'Failed - press [SPACE]' printed over the\nnormal screen; bit 3 of port $7FFD set, which shows bank 7's screen, and both screens'\nattributes set to $38 so the text shows. The answer ($28CF: ENTER passes) is recorded in IX;\nthen the screen cleared, the paging byte put back, cleared again, interrupts on.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "11374": {"comment":"No interrupts while paging"},
        "11375": {"comment":"Attributes all 0: black on black"},
        "11381": {"comment":"All $0300 attribute bytes"},
        "11388": {"comment":"Title, not yet visible"},
        "11394": {"comment":"'Passed - press [ENTER]'"},
        "11400": {"comment":"Paging byte kept"},
        "11404": {"comment":"RAM bank 7 at $C000"},
        "11406": {"comment":"And its copy"},
        "11409": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "11414": {"comment":"The screen copied to bank 7's"},
        "11420": {"comment":"$1800 bytes: the pixels"},
        "11425": {"comment":"Title again, on the normal screen"},
        "11431": {"comment":"'Failed - press [SPACE]' over it"},
        "11437": {"comment":"Bit 3: bank 7's screen shown"},
        "11442": {"comment":"And its copy"},
        "11445": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "11450": {"comment":"Normal screen's attributes $38"},
        "11459": {"comment":"$38: black INK on white PAPER"},
        "11463": {"comment":"Bank 7's too"},
        "11472": {"comment":"$38 there too"},
        "11476": {"comment":"ENTER (carry) or SPACE"},
        "11479": {"comment":"Result into IX"},
        "11482": {"comment":"Screen cleared"},
        "11485": {"comment":"Paging byte back"},
        "11486": {"comment":"Its copy"},
        "11489": {"comment":"Port $7FFD: bank and screen as before"},
        "11494": {"comment":"Cleared again, the normal screen"},
        "11497": {"comment":"Interrupts back on"},
        "11499": {"synopsis":"SCREEN_TEST's title: AT 8,3, PAPER 0, INK 0, 'Screen switching test'."},
        "11528": {"synopsis":"AT 12,3, PAPER 0, INK 0, 'Passed - press [ENTER]': seen on the second screen."},
        "11558": {"synopsis":"The same place: 'Failed - press [SPACE]', seen on the normal screen."},
        "11588": {"synopsis":"The cassette output test: the screen cleared, border red, BORDCR = $08, the title\n(CASS_OUT_MSG); a tone of $0A00 cycles with HL = $0100 sent to the MIC output (port $FE bit\n3) by an inline copy of TONE_OUT's loop that flips bit 3 and holds the speaker bit set;\nthen HEARD_TONE_MSG and the answer ($28CF: ENTER passes).\nExit: through $2641, the result into IX.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "11591": {"comment":"Border 2: red"},
        "11595": {"comment":"BORDCR = $08: border 1 in the tone"},
        "11600": {"comment":"CASSETTE OUTPUT TEST title"},
        "11606": {"comment":"HL = $0100, DE = $0A00 cycles"},
        "11612": {"comment":"No interrupts: exact timing"},
        "11613": {"comment":"IX kept (the results)"},
        "11615": {"comment":"L's low bits: 0-3 extra NOPs"},
        "11616": {"comment":"L / 4: the inner count"},
        "11620": {"comment":"IX = MIC_TONE_NOPS + 3 - low bits"},
        "11626": {"comment":"From MIC_TONE_NOPS"},
        "11630": {"comment":"+ 3 - low bits"},
        "11632": {"comment":"Border from BORDCR"},
        "11635": {"comment":"Bits 3-5: the border colour"},
        "11637": {"comment":"Down to bits 0-2"},
        "11640": {"comment":"Speaker bit 4 held set"},
        "11642": {"synopsis":"The entry JP (IX) uses: 0 to 3 NOPs, then the delay.","comment":"0-3 of these run, by IX"},
        "11645": {"comment":"B, C one more for the first DEC"},
        "11647": {"synopsis":"A half-cycle's delay: C inner rounds, B outer ones.","comment":"Inner delay"},
        "11648": {"comment":"Inner rounds"},
        "11650": {"comment":"C = $3F for the later rounds"},
        "11652": {"comment":"Outer count"},
        "11653": {"comment":"Outer rounds"},
        "11656": {"comment":"MIC bit 3 flipped"},
        "11658": {"comment":"Out: MIC flipped"},
        "11660": {"comment":"Outer count again; port byte in C"},
        "11662": {"comment":"MIC bit now set?"},
        "11664": {"comment":"Rising edge: the longer half"},
        "11666": {"comment":"Cycles left?"},
        "11668": {"comment":"None: done"},
        "11670": {"comment":"Port byte back, inner count from L"},
        "11672": {"comment":"One cycle fewer"},
        "11673": {"comment":"Next half-cycle"},
        "11675": {"synopsis":"After a rising edge: the second half-cycle, one inner count longer.","comment":"One inner count longer"},
        "11679": {"synopsis":"The cycles done: IX back; the question and the answer.","comment":"IX back"},
        "11681": {"comment":"BC = $1200 (not read by the printer)"},
        "11684": {"comment":"Heard the tone?"},
        "11690": {"comment":"ENTER (carry) or SPACE"},
        "11693": {"comment":"Result into IX"},
        "11697": {"synopsis":"The test program's verdict (jumped to after the last test): the 16 results in IX, a bit\neach. All set: border green, ALL_PASSED_MSG. Otherwise border red, TEST_FAILED_MSG and, for\nevery bit that is 0, its message from FAIL_MSGS (E's bits 0-7, then D's). Then REPEAT_MSG\nand a wait: ENTER is ignored, SPACE (BREAK) restarts the machine at $0000.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "11700": {"comment":"DE = the 16 results"},
        "11703": {"comment":"All bits set?"},
        "11705": {"comment":"$FF only when both are"},
        "11707": {"comment":"No: something failed"},
        "11709": {"comment":"Border 4: green"},
        "11713": {"comment":"'ALL TESTS PASSED'"},
        "11719": {"comment":"On to the repeat prompt"},
        "11721": {"synopsis":"Something failed: the failed tests listed.","comment":"Border 2: red"},
        "11723": {"comment":"Border written"},
        "11725": {"comment":"'TEST FAILED, because:-'"},
        "11731": {"comment":"BC = $0807 (B counted, not read)"},
        "11734": {"comment":"The results again"},
        "11736": {"comment":"Results again"},
        "11737": {"comment":"Kept for D's turn"},
        "11738": {"comment":"FAIL_MSGS: E's bits first"},
        "11741": {"comment":"Eight bits"},
        "11743": {"synopsis":"One bit of E: its message when it is 0.","comment":"Next bit: passed?"},
        "11745": {"comment":"Yes: no message"},
        "11747": {"comment":"Entry and count kept"},
        "11749": {"comment":"The message's address"},
        "11751": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "11753": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "11756": {"comment":"Count and entry back"},
        "11758": {"synopsis":"The next entry.","comment":"Next entry"},
        "11760": {"comment":"Count down"},
        "11761": {"comment":"More bits"},
        "11763": {"comment":"D's bits now"},
        "11764": {"comment":"E = D's results"},
        "11765": {"comment":"Eight bits"},
        "11767": {"synopsis":"One bit of D: its message when it is 0.","comment":"Next bit: passed?"},
        "11769": {"comment":"Yes: no message"},
        "11771": {"comment":"Entry, count, BC kept"},
        "11774": {"comment":"The message's address"},
        "11775": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "11778": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "11781": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "11784": {"comment":"D's failures counted in B"},
        "11785": {"synopsis":"The next entry.","comment":"Next entry"},
        "11787": {"comment":"Count down"},
        "11788": {"comment":"More bits"},
        "11790": {"synopsis":"The repeat prompt and the wait.","comment":"'Hold [BREAK] to repeat tests'"},
        "11793": {"comment":"BC = $1000 (not read by the printer)"},
        "11799": {"synopsis":"Waits for SPACE; ENTER is ignored.","comment":"ENTER (carry) or SPACE"},
        "11802": {"comment":"ENTER: wait again"},
        "11804": {"comment":"SPACE: restart the machine"},
        "11805": {"comment":"$0000: the machine starts again"},
        "11808": {"synopsis":"Two new lines and 'Hold [BREAK] to repeat tests'."},
        "11839": {"synopsis":"The RS232 test, through the sound chip's register 14 (its I/O port) and a loopback\nconnector: $FF, $FE, $FD, $FB and $F7 are written and must read back as $FF, $7E, $BD, $DB\nand $E7, so bit 0 must come back on bit 7, 1 on 6, 2 on 5 and 3 on 4. Nothing is printed.\nExit: through $2641, the result into IX: carry when every value read back right.","comment":"AY: C = $FD; B = $FF selects, $BF writes"},
        "11845": {"comment":"Register 14 selected"},
        "11846": {"comment":"Register 14"},
        "11850": {"comment":"$FF written"},
        "11852": {"comment":"B = $BF: write"},
        "11855": {"comment":"Read back"},
        "11858": {"comment":"$FF?"},
        "11860": {"comment":"No: failed"},
        "11862": {"comment":"Bit 0 low"},
        "11865": {"comment":"Written"},
        "11867": {"comment":"Read back"},
        "11870": {"comment":"Bits 0 and 7 low: $7E?"},
        "11872": {"comment":"No: failed"},
        "11874": {"comment":"Bit 1 low"},
        "11877": {"comment":"Written"},
        "11879": {"comment":"Read back"},
        "11882": {"comment":"Bits 1 and 6 low: $BD?"},
        "11884": {"comment":"No: failed"},
        "11886": {"comment":"Bit 2 low"},
        "11889": {"comment":"Written"},
        "11891": {"comment":"Read back"},
        "11894": {"comment":"Bits 2 and 5 low: $DB?"},
        "11896": {"comment":"No: failed"},
        "11898": {"comment":"Bit 3 low"},
        "11901": {"comment":"Written"},
        "11903": {"comment":"Read back"},
        "11906": {"comment":"Bits 3 and 4 low: $E7?"},
        "11908": {"comment":"No: failed"},
        "11910": {"comment":"All right: passed"},
        "11914": {"synopsis":"A value read back wrong: no carry.","comment":"Failed: no carry"},
        "11918": {"synopsis":"The ULA sound test: the screen cleared, border red, BORDCR = $08, the title\n(ULA_SOUND_MSG); a tone on the speaker (TONE_OUT through $2946: HL = $0100, DE = $0A00);\nHEARD_TONE_MSG and the answer ($28CF: ENTER passes).\nExit: through $2641, the result into IX.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "11921": {"comment":"Border 2: red"},
        "11925": {"comment":"BORDCR = $08: border 1 in the tone"},
        "11930": {"comment":"ULA SOUND TEST title"},
        "11936": {"comment":"HL = $0100, DE = $0A00 cycles"},
        "11939": {"comment":"$0A00 cycles"},
        "11942": {"comment":"TONE_OUT, then DI"},
        "11945": {"comment":"BC = $1200 (not read by the printer)"},
        "11948": {"comment":"Heard the tone?"},
        "11954": {"comment":"ENTER (carry) or SPACE"},
        "11957": {"comment":"Result into IX"},
        "11961": {"synopsis":"The sound chip test: the screen cleared, border cyan, the title (GI_SOUND_MSG); the\nregisters set from AY_SETTINGS; the tones of channels A, B and C each alone for 40 frames\n(mixer $FE, $FD, $FB), then all three together (mixer $F8) for 40 more, then the mixer $FF\n(all off); FOUR_SOUNDS_MSG and the answer ($28CF: ENTER passes).\nExit: through $2641, the result into IX.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "11964": {"comment":"Border 5: cyan"},
        "11968": {"comment":"GI SOUND TEST title"},
        "11974": {"comment":"AY: C = $FD; B = $FF selects, $BF writes"},
        "11980": {"comment":"Register/value pairs"},
        "11983": {"synopsis":"One register/value pair, until a byte with bit 7 set.","comment":"Register number"},
        "11985": {"comment":"The end marker?"},
        "11987": {"comment":"Yes: the mixer next"},
        "11989": {"comment":"Selected"},
        "11990": {"comment":"Out"},
        "11992": {"comment":"Its value"},
        "11994": {"comment":"Written"},
        "11995": {"comment":"Out"},
        "11997": {"comment":"Next pair"},
        "11999": {"synopsis":"The four sounds.","comment":"AY ports again"},
        "12005": {"comment":"Three channels, one at a time"},
        "12007": {"comment":"Mixer $FE: tone A only"},
        "12009": {"synopsis":"One channel's tone alone for 40 frames.","comment":"Register 7 selected"},
        "12010": {"comment":"Register 7"},
        "12014": {"comment":"Mixer written"},
        "12015": {"comment":"Out: mixer value H"},
        "12017": {"comment":"Kept round the wait"},
        "12020": {"comment":"40 frames"},
        "12026": {"comment":"Next channel: $FD, then $FB"},
        "12027": {"comment":"Carry into bit 0, next bit out"},
        "12029": {"comment":"Count down"},
        "12030": {"comment":"More channels"},
        "12032": {"comment":"Mixer $F8: all three tones"},
        "12034": {"comment":"Register 7 selected"},
        "12039": {"comment":"Written"},
        "12042": {"comment":"Kept round the wait"},
        "12045": {"comment":"40 frames"},
        "12048": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "12051": {"comment":"Mixer $FF: all off"},
        "12053": {"comment":"Register 7 selected"},
        "12058": {"comment":"$FF written"},
        "12059": {"comment":"Written"},
        "12061": {"comment":"BC = $0A00 (not read by the printer)"},
        "12064": {"comment":"Heard four sounds?"},
        "12070": {"comment":"ENTER (carry) or SPACE"},
        "12073": {"comment":"Result into IX"},
        "12076": {"synopsis":"The sound chip's registers for COLOUR_BARS and GI_SOUND_TEST, as register/value pairs\nended by $80: tone periods A $0040, B $0080, C $0100; noise period $1F; volumes A, B and C\n15. Read at $2B5C and $2ECF."},
        "12097": {"synopsis":"The question after the ULA sound and cassette output tones: 'Press [ENTER] if you heard\nthe tone, else press [SPACE]'."},
        "12154": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 15 (D bit 7 of the results): the colour test's failure line, ended by a new\nline."},
        "12174": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 7 (E bit 7 of the results): the ULA sound test's failure line, ended by a\nnew line."},
        "12197": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 10 (D bit 2 of the results): the SYMBOL SHIFT/A test's failure line, ended\nby a new line."},
        "12224": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 9 (D bit 1 of the results): the ULA test's failure line, ended by a new\nline."},
        "12241": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 8 (D bit 0 of the results): the RS232 test's failure line, ended by a new\nline."},
        "12260": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 11 (D bit 3 of the results): the sound chip test's failure line, ended by a\nnew line."},
        "12282": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 12 (D bit 4 of the results): the RAM paging test's failure line, ended by a\nnew line."},
        "12308": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 6 (E bit 6 of the results): the joystick test's failure line, ended by a new\nline."},
        "12330": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 14 (D bit 6 of the results): the IC 7 checksum's failure line, ended by a\nnew line."},
        "12352": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 13 (D bit 5 of the results): the IC 8 checksum's failure line, ended by a\nnew line."},
        "12374": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 1 (E bit 1 of the results): the disk test's failure line, ended by a new\nline."},
        "12393": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 4 (E bit 4 of the results): the second screen test's failure line, ended by\na new line."},
        "12420": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 5 (E bit 5 of the results): the cassette output test's failure line, ended\nby a new line."},
        "12444": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 0 (E bit 0 of the results): the cassette input test's failure line, ended by\na new line."},
        "12467": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 3 (E bit 3 of the results): the printer BUSY test's failure line, ended by a\nnew line."},
        "12493": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 2 (E bit 2 of the results): the printer DATA test's failure line, ended by a\nnew line."},
        "12519": {"synopsis":"TEST_REPORT's failure lines, one word per result bit: entries 0-7 for E's bits 0-7 (IX's\nlow byte), 8-15 for D's. In order: cassette input, disk, printer DATA, printer BUSY, second\nscreen, cassette output, joystick, ULA sound; RS232, ULA, SYMBOL SHIFT/A, sound chip, RAM\npaging, IC 8, IC 7, colour. The first test shifted into IX ends up in D's bit 7, the last\nin E's bit 0. Read at $2DE5 and $2DFE."},
        "12551": {"synopsis":"AT 5,5, FLASH 1, 'ROM TEST FAILED', FLASH 0 and a new line. No code in this ROM loads its\naddress."},
        "12575": {"synopsis":"AT 5,5, FLASH 1, 'RAM TEST FAILED', FLASH 0 and a new line. No code in this ROM loads its\naddress."},
        "12599": {"synopsis":"The keyboard test's screen (printed at $297C): AT 2,0, the title, then INVERSE 1 and the\nkeyboard drawn row by row as letters two columns apart, a lower-case letter for each key\nwithout a single character of its own (the CAPS SHIFT and SYMBOL SHIFT combinations of\nKEY_TEST_CODES, the two shifts, ENTER, BREAK); INVERSE 0, then AT 20,5, FLASH 1, 'TEST ALL\nTHE KEYS'."},
        "13049": {"synopsis":"SYMA_TEST's screen: AT 5,5, INVERSE 1 ' SYM SHFT/A  TEST ', and at rows 10-14 'Press',\n'SYM SHFT/A' (flashing) and 'for 1 sec'."},
        "13118": {"synopsis":"COLOUR_TEST's screen: AT 9,0, INVERSE 1, the test program's title and version line, 'Check\nTV tuning', a reminder to fit the loopback connector, the ENTER/SPACE question about the\ncolours, and a flashing warning that the tests corrupt disks and need factory equipment."},
        "13422": {"synopsis":"AT 5,5, INVERSE 1, ' ULA TEST ', INVERSE 0, a new line."},
        "13441": {"synopsis":"AT 5,7, INVERSE 1, 'RAM DATA TESTS', AT 10,5, '.. STARTING NOW ..', INVERSE 0, a new line."},
        "13485": {"synopsis":"AT 5,5, INVERSE 1, ' GI SOUND TEST ', two new lines, INVERSE 0."},
        "13510": {"synopsis":"AT 5,5, INVERSE 1, ' ULA SOUND TEST ', two new lines, INVERSE 0."},
        "13536": {"synopsis":"A 0 before CASS_OUT_MSG; the print starts after it."},
        "13537": {"synopsis":"AT 5,5, INVERSE 1, 'CASSETTE OUTPUT TEST', INVERSE 0, two new lines."},
        "13567": {"synopsis":"A 0 before JOY_TEST_MSG; the print starts after it."},
        "13568": {"synopsis":"JOYSTICK_TEST's screen: AT 0,10, INVERSE 1 'JOYSTICK TEST', the instructions (move both\njoysticks and press fire until the letters are wiped out; SPACE gives up) and a box drawn\nwith + - ! holding the J1 and J2 labels UP, LF, FI, RI and DN."},
        "13967": {"synopsis":"AT 5,5, ' ALL TESTS PASSED ', a new line."},
        "13990": {"synopsis":"AT 0,0, FLASH 1, ' TEST FAILED, because:- ', FLASH 0, two new lines."},
        "14024": {"synopsis":"GI_SOUND_TEST's question: 'press [ENTER] if you heard four sounds, else press [SPACE].'"},
        "14089": {"synopsis":"Makes a tone on the speaker (port $FE bit 4) for the test program, with the border in\nBORDCR's colour (its bits 3-5) and the MIC bit 3 set in every write: about DE cycles, each\nhalf-cycle a delay set by HL (H counts the outer loop, L / 4 the inner one, and L's low two\nbits pick an entry into TONE_NOPS for the finest step). Interrupts are off while it runs and\nturned on at the end. $2946 calls it.\nEntry: HL = the pitch, DE = the cycles.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"No interrupts: exact timing"},
        "14090": {"comment":"IX kept (the results)"},
        "14092": {"comment":"L's low bits: 0-3 extra NOPs"},
        "14093": {"comment":"L / 4: the inner count"},
        "14095": {"comment":"Inner count in L"},
        "14097": {"comment":"IX = TONE_NOPS + 3 - low bits"},
        "14098": {"comment":"3 - low bits"},
        "14103": {"comment":"From TONE_NOPS"},
        "14107": {"comment":"+ 3 - low bits"},
        "14109": {"comment":"Border from BORDCR"},
        "14112": {"comment":"Bits 3-5: the border colour"},
        "14114": {"comment":"Down to bits 0-2"},
        "14117": {"comment":"MIC bit 3 held set"},
        "14119": {"synopsis":"The entry JP (IX) uses: 0 to 3 NOPs, then the delay.","comment":"0-3 of these run, by IX"},
        "14122": {"comment":"B, C one more for the first DEC"},
        "14124": {"synopsis":"A half-cycle's delay: C inner rounds, B outer ones.","comment":"Inner delay"},
        "14125": {"comment":"Inner rounds"},
        "14127": {"comment":"C = $3F for the later rounds"},
        "14129": {"comment":"Outer count"},
        "14130": {"comment":"Outer rounds"},
        "14133": {"comment":"Speaker bit 4 flipped"},
        "14135": {"comment":"Out: speaker flipped"},
        "14137": {"comment":"Outer count again; port byte in C"},
        "14139": {"comment":"Speaker bit now set?"},
        "14141": {"comment":"Rising edge: the longer half"},
        "14143": {"comment":"Cycles left?"},
        "14145": {"comment":"None: done"},
        "14147": {"comment":"Port byte back, inner count from L"},
        "14149": {"comment":"One cycle fewer"},
        "14150": {"comment":"Next half-cycle"},
        "14152": {"synopsis":"After a rising edge: the second half-cycle, one inner count longer.","comment":"One inner count longer"},
        "14154": {"comment":"Next half-cycle"},
        "14156": {"synopsis":"The cycles done: interrupts on, IX back.","comment":"Interrupts back on"},
        "14157": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "14160": {"synopsis":"Where JOYSTICK_TEST's ten labels are, as row/column pairs with the row 3 more than the\nscreen row: joystick 1's FI, UP, DN, RI, LF (D's bits 0-4), then joystick 2's LF, RI, DN,\nUP, FI (E's bits 0-4). Read at $2C27 and $2C49."},
        "14180": {"synopsis":"The ten labels' names in JOY_PLACES's order, two letters each, no end marker. Nothing in\nthis ROM reads them."},
        "14200": {"synopsis":"The disk test: DISK_TEST_RAM copied to $5F00 and run there, since it pages this ROM out.\nExit: through $2641, the drive test's carry into IX.","comment":"From DISK_TEST_RAM"},
        "14203": {"comment":"To $5F00"},
        "14206": {"comment":"$3D bytes"},
        "14211": {"comment":"Run there"},
        "14214": {"synopsis":"Runs at $5F00 (DISK_TEST copies it):\n1. Port $1FFD = 4: ROM 2 paged in.\n2. $0C00 bytes of\nROM 2 from $2492 (its drive test program, DT_START) copied to $6000.\n3. Port $1FFD = 0 and\nport $7FFD = $10, with their copies $5B67 and $5B5C: ROM 1 and RAM bank 0.\n4. Interrupts\non, the copy called at $6000, IX kept round it.\n5. Port $7FFD = 0 ($5B5C too): this ROM\nback; the copy's carry into IX through $2641.","comment":"$1FFD bit 2: ROM 2 in"},
        "14216": {"comment":"Port $1FFD"},
        "14221": {"comment":"ROM 2's drive test program"},
        "14224": {"comment":"To $6000"},
        "14227": {"comment":"$0C00 bytes"},
        "14230": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "14232": {"comment":"Port $1FFD = 0"},
        "14234": {"comment":"Port $1FFD"},
        "14239": {"comment":"And its copy"},
        "14242": {"comment":"Port $7FFD = $10: ROM 1, bank 0"},
        "14244": {"comment":"B = $7F: port $7FFD"},
        "14248": {"comment":"And its copy"},
        "14251": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "14252": {"comment":"IX kept (the results)"},
        "14254": {"comment":"The drive test"},
        "14257": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "14259": {"comment":"Its result kept"},
        "14260": {"comment":"Port $7FFD = 0: this ROM back"},
        "14262": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "14267": {"comment":"And its copy"},
        "14270": {"comment":"The result"},
        "14271": {"comment":"Into IX"},
        "14275": {"synopsis":"The cassette input test: the instructions (TAPE_TEST_MSG) and a 25-frame pause (CI_WAIT);\nwith interrupts off, six black marks across attribute row 7 (columns 1, 7, ... 31); then,\nround after round, the EAR input (port $FE bit 6) polled $1000 times and its changes\ncounted, the count / 32 (at most 32) shown as a bright cyan cell over a bright blue row 8;\nuntil ENTER (passed) or SPACE (failed) is pressed.\nExit: through CI_WAIT after the result went into IX.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "14278": {"comment":"Instructions"},
        "14281": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "14284": {"comment":"25 frames' pause"},
        "14287": {"comment":"No interrupts while counting"},
        "14288": {"comment":"Row 7, column 1"},
        "14291": {"comment":"Every sixth cell"},
        "14294": {"comment":"Six marks, attribute 0"},
        "14296": {"synopsis":"One mark.","comment":"A black cell"},
        "14297": {"comment":"Six cells on"},
        "14298": {"comment":"Next mark"},
        "14300": {"synopsis":"One round: $1000 polls of the EAR input and the keys, then the reading shown.","comment":"Changes counted in HL"},
        "14303": {"comment":"$1000 polls"},
        "14306": {"comment":"C = $FE: no level yet"},
        "14308": {"comment":"SPACE pressed?"},
        "14310": {"comment":"Row $7FFE"},
        "14312": {"comment":"Bit 0: SPACE"},
        "14314": {"comment":"Yes: failed"},
        "14317": {"comment":"ENTER pressed?"},
        "14320": {"comment":"Row $BFFE"},
        "14322": {"comment":"Bit 0: ENTER"},
        "14324": {"comment":"Yes: passed"},
        "14327": {"synopsis":"One poll of the EAR input.","comment":"Count the polls down"},
        "14330": {"comment":"Done: show the reading"},
        "14332": {"comment":"EAR level (bit 6)"},
        "14334": {"comment":"Only bit 6"},
        "14336": {"comment":"Same as last time?"},
        "14337": {"comment":"Same: next poll"},
        "14339": {"comment":"Changed: counted"},
        "14340": {"comment":"New level kept"},
        "14341": {"comment":"Next poll"},
        "14343": {"synopsis":"The reading: the changes / 32, at most 32.","comment":"HL x 8: H = changes / 32"},
        "14355": {"comment":"L = the reading"},
        "14356": {"comment":"Over 32?"},
        "14358": {"comment":"Compared with H"},
        "14361": {"comment":"Kept at 32"},
        "14363": {"synopsis":"Row 8 redrawn after a frame and the marker set at the reading's column.","comment":"HL = the reading"},
        "14364": {"comment":"H = 0"},
        "14365": {"comment":"Row 8's last cell"},
        "14368": {"comment":"32 cells"},
        "14370": {"comment":"$48: bright blue paper"},
        "14372": {"comment":"Wait for a frame"},
        "14373": {"comment":"One frame"},
        "14374": {"comment":"Interrupts off again"},
        "14375": {"synopsis":"One cell.","comment":"Row 8 filled, right to left"},
        "14377": {"comment":"32 cells"},
        "14379": {"comment":"DE = row 8's first cell"},
        "14380": {"comment":"The reading's cell"},
        "14381": {"comment":"$68: bright cyan marker"},
        "14383": {"comment":"Marker written"},
        "14384": {"comment":"Next round"},
        "14386": {"synopsis":"A 25-frame pause with interrupts on, then FLAGS bit 5 (a new key) cleared.\nExit: carry; interrupts on.\nChanges: B, HL, F.","comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "14387": {"comment":"25 frames"},
        "14389": {"synopsis":"One frame."},
        "14390": {"comment":"25 times"},
        "14392": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 5 cleared: no key waiting"},
        "14397": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "14398": {"comment":"Done"},
        "14399": {"synopsis":"SPACE: no carry into IX (failed); the pause; out of CASS_IN_TEST.","comment":"No carry: failed"},
        "14400": {"comment":"Into IX"},
        "14403": {"comment":"Pause, then out"},
        "14405": {"synopsis":"ENTER: carry into IX (passed); the pause; out of CASS_IN_TEST.","comment":"Carry: passed"},
        "14406": {"comment":"Into IX"},
        "14409": {"comment":"Pause, then out"},
        "14411": {"synopsis":"CASS_IN_TEST's instructions: AT 0,0, insert the test tape and press PLAY, adjust the\nazimuth screw for the largest reading, then ENTER for success or SPACE for failure."},
        "14554": {"synopsis":"Bytes nothing in this ROM reads, up to $39CD. Each byte XORed with $30 and with bit 7\ndropped gives, for most of them, a credits text with lines ended by $0D: who did the test\nprogram, thanks, and the machines and tools it was written with. Some bytes, mostly near\nthe end, do not decode that way."},
        "14798": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to $3DFF."},
        "15872": {"synopsis":"ROM 2's CALL_ROM0, of which these are the same bytes: it parks AF and HL at $5B56 and\n$5B52, reads the word after the CALL into HL (stepping the return address past it) and\nclears bit 2 of port $1FFD (and $5B67) with interrupts off. That OUT, at $3E1C, pages this\nROM in, so the code goes on here at $3E1E: CALL_ROM0_BACK is pushed as the return, AF and\nHL are restored and the RET jumps to the address. Nothing in this ROM calls it.","comment":"HL parked"},
        "15875": {"comment":"AF parked"},
        "15877": {"comment":"At $5B56"},
        "15880": {"comment":"The word after the CALL"},
        "15881": {"comment":"BC = the address"},
        "15885": {"comment":"Return address stepped past it"},
        "15886": {"comment":"HL = the address"},
        "15888": {"comment":"Bit 2 of port $1FFD cleared: ROM 0"},
        "15894": {"comment":"Bit 2 cleared"},
        "15897": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "15900": {"comment":"ROM 0 in: on at $3E1E here"},
        "15902": {"comment":"From here in this ROM"},
        "15903": {"comment":"The way back first"},
        "15907": {"comment":"Then the address"},
        "15908": {"comment":"AF and HL back"},
        "15912": {"comment":"AF from $5B56"},
        "15913": {"comment":"HL from $5B52"},
        "15916": {"comment":"To the address"},
        "15917": {"synopsis":"Where a routine called through CALL_ROM0 returns: bit 2 of port $1FFD (and $5B67) set\nagain with interrupts off, keeping AF and BC; after the OUT at $3E3B the code goes on in ROM\n2's copy.","comment":"BC and AF kept"},
        "15919": {"comment":"Bit 2 of port $1FFD set: ROM 2"},
        "15925": {"comment":"Bit 2 set"},
        "15928": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "15931": {"comment":"ROM 2 in: on at $3E3D there"},
        "15933": {"comment":"From here in ROM 2"},
        "15934": {"comment":"AF and BC back"},
        "15937": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to $3E7F."},
        "16000": {"synopsis":"Calls the address in the word after the CALL in ROM 1, keeping AF, BC and HL (parked at\n$5B56, $5B54 and $5B52): the word is read into HL and the return address stepped past it;\nbit 4 of the paging byte $5B5C (port $7FFD) is set with interrupts off, which pages ROM 1\nin, and the code goes on at $3EA2 in ROM 1's copy; CALL_ROM1_BACK is pushed as the return,\nAF, BC and HL are restored and the RET jumps to the address. The return runs ROM 1's\n$3EB5, which clears the bit again. ROM 1 has the same routine here with the bit cleared,\nfor its calls into this ROM. Called at $028A, $08FE, $092D, $0947, $0DB0 and $212A.","comment":"HL parked"},
        "16003": {"comment":"BC parked"},
        "16007": {"comment":"AF parked"},
        "16009": {"comment":"At $5B56"},
        "16012": {"comment":"The word after the CALL"},
        "16013": {"comment":"BC = the address"},
        "16017": {"comment":"Return address stepped past it"},
        "16018": {"comment":"HL = the address"},
        "16020": {"comment":"Bit 4 of port $7FFD set: ROM 1"},
        "16023": {"comment":"Bit 4 set"},
        "16026": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "16032": {"comment":"ROM 1 in: on at $3EA2 there"},
        "16034": {"comment":"From here in ROM 1"},
        "16035": {"comment":"The way back first"},
        "16039": {"comment":"Then the address"},
        "16040": {"comment":"AF, BC and HL back"},
        "16044": {"comment":"AF from $5B56"},
        "16045": {"comment":"BC from $5B54"},
        "16049": {"comment":"HL from $5B52"},
        "16052": {"comment":"To the address"},
        "16053": {"synopsis":"Where a routine of this ROM called through ROM 1's copy of CALL_ROM1 returns: bit 4 of\n$5B5C (port $7FFD) set again with interrupts off, which pages ROM 1 back in, keeping AF and\nBC; the code after the OUT at $3EC3 runs in ROM 1.","comment":"AF and BC kept"},
        "16055": {"comment":"Bit 4 of port $7FFD set: ROM 1"},
        "16058": {"comment":"Bit 4 set"},
        "16061": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "16067": {"comment":"ROM 1 in: on at $3EC5 there"},
        "16069": {"comment":"From here in ROM 1"},
        "16070": {"comment":"BC and AF back"},
        "16073": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to $3EFF."},
        "16128": {"synopsis":"ROM 1's CALL_ROM2, of which these are the same bytes, and of which this ROM runs the middle:\nROM 1 parks HL, BC and AF at $5B52, $5B54 and $5B56, reads the word after the CALL and\nclears bit 4 of port $7FFD (and $5B5C); that OUT, at $3F20, pages this ROM in, so\n$3F22-$3F2D\nrun here and set bit 2 of port $1FFD (and $5B67), which pages ROM 2 in, where the code goes\non at $3F2F. Nothing in this ROM calls it.","comment":"HL parked"},
        "16131": {"comment":"BC parked"},
        "16135": {"comment":"AF parked"},
        "16137": {"comment":"At $5B56"},
        "16140": {"comment":"The word after the CALL"},
        "16141": {"comment":"BC = the address"},
        "16145": {"comment":"Return address stepped past it"},
        "16146": {"comment":"HL = the address"},
        "16148": {"comment":"Bit 4 of port $7FFD cleared: ROM 0"},
        "16151": {"comment":"Bit 4 cleared"},
        "16154": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "16160": {"comment":"ROM 0 in: on at $3F22 here"},
        "16162": {"comment":"From here in this ROM: bit 2 of $1FFD set"},
        "16165": {"comment":"Bit 2 set"},
        "16170": {"comment":"Port $1FFD"},
        "16173": {"comment":"ROM 2 in: on at $3F2F there"},
        "16175": {"comment":"From here in ROM 2"},
        "16176": {"comment":"The way back first"},
        "16180": {"comment":"Then the address"},
        "16181": {"comment":"AF, BC and HL back"},
        "16185": {"comment":"AF from $5B56"},
        "16186": {"comment":"BC from $5B54"},
        "16190": {"comment":"HL from $5B52"},
        "16193": {"comment":"To the address"},
        "16194": {"synopsis":"The way back from ROM 2 to ROM 1, keeping AF and BC: ROM 2 clears bit 2 of port $1FFD (and\n$5B67), which pages this ROM in, so $3F52-$3F5D run here and set bit 4 of port $7FFD (and\n$5B5C), which pages ROM 1 back in for the RET.","comment":"BC and AF kept"},
        "16196": {"comment":"Bit 2 of port $1FFD cleared: ROM 0"},
        "16199": {"comment":"Bit 2 cleared"},
        "16202": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "16208": {"comment":"ROM 0 in: on at $3F52 here"},
        "16210": {"comment":"From here in this ROM: bit 4 set"},
        "16213": {"comment":"Bit 4 set"},
        "16218": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "16221": {"comment":"ROM 1 in: on at $3F5F there"},
        "16223": {"comment":"From here in ROM 1"},
        "16224": {"comment":"AF and BC back"},
        "16227": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to $3FEF."},
        "16368": {"synopsis":"ROM 2's way into this ROM: its ROM0_HOOK_A0 and ROM0_HOOK_A call $3FF0 through CALL_ROM0.\nIt jumps to $21A3 (PROMPT_KEY), which takes the zero flag, A, HL and DE as ROM 2 passes\nthem.","comment":"On to $21A3"},
        "16371": {"synopsis":"Unused: $FF up to $3FFE."},
        "16383": {"synopsis":"The last byte, $B6. Nothing in this ROM's code reads it."}
      }
    }
  },
